==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
Derived from {{m|non|systir||sister}} (or more correctly an old adjectival form of it, {{m|non|*swes(t)riga-}})<ref>[https://malid.is/leit/systkini Íslensk orðsifjabók]</ref> with the suffix {{m|non|*-īn(i)a}} indicating a relation between people as in the words {{m|non|feðgin||a father and his daughter}} and {{m|non|mæðgin||a mother and her son}}.<ref>[https://archive.org/details/nordischesetymologischesworterbuch/page/n625/mode/2up Altnordisches Etymologisches Wörterbuch, 1977]</ref><ref>[https://books.google.is/books?id=QlBOJPI5YosC&pg=PA518&lpg=PA518&dq=swestrigin&source=bl&ots=_Q7E0V7tQU&sig=ACfU3U2c6o8ywD4YynR4P_7MRmqVsL-9GA&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwj1jciw1eP1AhXOYMAKHUEFBbAQ6AF6BAgUEAM#v=onepage&q=swestrigin&f=false Reallexikon der germanischen Altertumskunde, Volume 11]</ref> Unrelated to the English {{m|en|kin}}.

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|non|systkini}}

===Noun===
{{non-noun|n-p}}

